  "patch": "r38-runtime.patch",
  "patch_sha256": "f22ac9c23fda597b7bf4e771316c70f4ea0d62fe843362e1399712cef8286424",
  "target_gpu_validation": "NOT_RUN; enforced by upgrade-time gates",
  "local_adaptations": [
    "Retain frozen SM80 graph-safe vision fallback, thread-local tokenizer protection, five-value layer ABI and int8 x_scales.",
    "Preserve trailing Anthropic system turns only when the tokenizer explicitly advertises inline system support; retain conservative fallback otherwise.",
    "Initialize DSpark broadcast weights at the end of the frozen load_weights lifecycle, after original _finalize_moe; no nonexistent process_weights_after_loading hook.",
    "Keep R3.4 loaded-weight WKV numeric checks on all TP ranks; add broadcast initialization logging and a GPU numeric/graph replay gate.",
    "Recognize top-level CustomTool in frozen parser name collection and schema generation; keep prior wrapper recovery and tool validation.",
    "Use streamed call_id when opening tool items and reuse completed streamed function/custom items in final Responses output.",
    "Retain zero-decode/empty-metadata guards around modulo-based ragged protection and use the same condition for packing/unpacking.",
    "Match installed OpenAI SDK ActionFind discriminator find_in_page; no new built-in browser tool execution.",
    "R3.6 preserves all 18 inherited R3.5 overlay files byte-for-byte, adds XGrammar EOS guards as file 19, and includes real XGrammar CPU regression before service stop.",
    "R3.7 retains all 19 inherited overlay files byte-for-byte; five new files cover tokenization, sparse metadata and greedy selection.",
    "Tool-history validation copies message dictionaries and materializes lazy Pydantic tool_calls before serialization; malformed calls fail validation.",
    "Use split argmax only in the frozen DSpark greedy non-local-reduction branch; keep k6, Markov dependencies, local-argmax configuration and verifier unchanged.",
    "Freeze the existing XGrammar feature gate: additional schema patches deferred after identifying the engine-level backend latch."
  ],
